<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Refurbished on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/refurbished/</link><description>Recent content in Refurbished on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:18:16 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/refurbished/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>My Addiction to Second-Hand and Refurbished Computers</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/second-hand-refurbished-computer-addiction/</link><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:18:16 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/second-hand-refurbished-computer-addiction/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ll admit it: I have a problem. Every time a second-hand or refurbished machine turns up cheap, I find a reason to buy it. The result is a small fleet of computers accumulating around the house, most of which I didn&amp;rsquo;t strictly need.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="wp-caption alignnone"&gt;&#10; &lt;a data-flickr-embed="true" data-header="true" data-footer="false"&#10; data-context="false"&#10; href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/55539966753"&#10; title="Fleet Ranking@2x"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/55539966753_2e1205ca81_z.jpg" width="800" alt="Fleet Ranking@2x" /&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;script async src="//embedr.flickr.com/assets/client-code.js" charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="wp-caption-text"&gt;Current home computer setup, not including work laptops.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s not really about the hardware itself, though. It&amp;rsquo;s an enjoyable side hobby — each new (old) machine is an excuse to play around with a different operating system, distro, or desktop environment without any risk to the computer I actually rely on day to day. Recently that meant putting &lt;a href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/omarchy-linux-on-an-old-laptop/"&gt;Omarchy Linux on an old laptop&lt;/a&gt; just to see how it held up.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>